  "body": "Opening here at the request of @domenic -- while looking into providing an [ImageDecoder API](https://github.com/dalecurtis/image-decoder-api/blob/master/explainer.md) I've hit an issue with streaming multipart MJPEG resources and the ReadableStream returned by response.body.\r\n\r\nDownstream streams don't know the multipart boundary specified in the Content-Type header, so they can't parse headers out of the ReadableStream to get at the binary data. E.g., Using [cam2web](https://github.com/cvsandbox/cam2web/), the multipart Content-Type is:\r\n\r\n> Content-Type=multipart/x-mixed-replace; boundary=--myboundary\r\n\r\nAnd each chunk of the response looks like this:\r\n\r\n> '--myboundary\\r\\nContent-Type: image/jpeg\\r\\nContent-Length: $SIZE\\r\\n\\r\\n$JPEG_DATA'\r\n\r\nSo multipart ReadableStreams today require a user supplied TransformStream to reform the data into contiguous blocks. @domenic indicated there may be some interest in providing a browser-supplied solution to this, so opening this issue for discussion. Thanks!",
